# Finding 1 of RESULTS.md: the worker is paused while transfers are acknowledged, then the power
# is cut. Lago's Redis runs without an append-only file, so the queued jobs that would make the
# fees are gone after the cut, and 4 of 9 acknowledged transfers are never charged. With
# `hydo build hydo.yaml --set redis_aof=yes` the same schedule passes.
# Found by the explorer (seed 8), in the seed form; the command list below is the one W= was
# drawn against.
# commands: anytime_redeliver eventually_1_billing_tick eventually_2_transfers_charged first_seed parallel_driver_batch parallel_driver_event serial_driver_terminate
# expect: violation
disk=cut dseed=629bfb2777cb6c08 | run C=10 P=api_worker@5+5 T=0:300 W=340bcd65,p1,q1,r3000
